---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { BUSINESS } from '../consts';

// Privacy policy. Two audiences: (1) real visitors, (2) mobile carriers
// reviewing the 10DLC/A2P campaign registration — carriers specifically look
// for an explicit statement that mobile numbers and SMS consent are never
// shared or sold for third-party marketing. That sentence is load-bearing;
// do not soften or remove it without checking A2P impact first.
//
// The legal entity is NGD Enterprises LLC; AITS is the brand it trades under.
// A legal document has to name the real entity, so it does not use
// SITE.legalName (which is the brand expansion, not the registered name).
const LEGAL_ENTITY = 'NGD Enterprises LLC';
const EFFECTIVE = 'August 18, 2026';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How AITS collects, uses, and protects your information — including our SMS messaging program, what we never share, and your privacy rights."
  path="/privacy"
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="section-label">Legal</span>
      <h1 class="section-heading">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="section-sub">
        Effective {EFFECTIVE}. This policy explains what we collect, why, and what we will
        never do with it.
      </p>

      <div class="prose policy">
        <p>
          This Privacy Policy applies to <strong>{LEGAL_ENTITY}</strong>, doing business as
          <strong>AITS</strong> ("AITS," "we," "us"), and to the website at
          <a href="https://aits.llc">aits.llc</a> and the tools we provide through it.
        </p>

        <div class="callout">
          <strong>The short version.</strong> We do not sell your personal information. We do not
          share your mobile number with anyone for their marketing. We collect what we need to
          answer you and deliver what you asked for, and nothing else.
        </div>

        <h2>Information we collect</h2>
        <p><strong>Information you give us.</strong> When you use the AI Risk Scan, subscribe to
        our newsletter, or contact us, we may collect your name, business name, business website,
        email address, phone number, your preferred contact method, and your answers to the
        assessment questions. Providing this is voluntary.</p>
        <p><strong>Information collected automatically.</strong> Like most websites, we receive
        standard technical data such as IP address, browser type, pages viewed, and referring page.
        We use Google Analytics for this. You can opt out with the
        <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google
        Analytics opt-out add-on</a>.</p>

        <h2>How we use it</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>To generate and deliver the report or information you requested.</li>
          <li>To respond to you and, if you asked us to, follow up about a consultation.</li>
          <li>To send the newsletter, if you subscribed. Every email has an unsubscribe link.</li>
          <li>To operate, secure, and improve the site.</li>
          <li>To meet legal and record-keeping obligations, including consent records.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2 id="sms">Text messaging (SMS)</h2>
        <p>
          We only text you if you checked the box giving express written consent. Consent is never
          required to receive a report, use the site, or buy anything from us. When you consent, we
          record the date, time, and the exact wording you agreed to.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>Messages relate to the assessment you requested and any consultation you schedule.</li>
          <li>Message frequency varies — typically 2 to 5 messages.</li>
          <li>Message and data rates may apply.</li>
          <li>Reply <strong>STOP</strong> at any time to opt out. Reply <strong>HELP</strong> for help.</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="callout callout-strong">
          <strong>We never share mobile information with third parties or affiliates for their
          marketing or promotional purposes.</strong> Mobile opt-in data and consent records are not
          sold, rented, or shared with anyone for marketing. Text-messaging originator opt-in data
          is not shared with any third party except the service providers strictly necessary to
          deliver the messages themselves.
        </div>

        <h2>Service providers</h2>
        <p>
          We use a small number of vendors to run the business — website hosting and security, email
          delivery, a customer relationship management platform, scheduling, and analytics. They may
          process your information only to perform services for us, under contract, and may not use
          it for their own purposes.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>AI processing.</strong> When you complete the AI Risk Scan, your answers and the
          resulting scores are sent to a third-party AI provider that generates a short written
          summary for your report. We do not send your name, email, or phone number for that step.
        </p>

        <h2>What we never do</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>We do not sell your personal information.</li>
          <li>We do not share your mobile number or SMS consent for anyone else's marketing.</li>
          <li>We do not send you texts you did not explicitly agree to receive.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          We may disclose information if required by law, to protect our rights or someone's safety,
          or as part of a business transfer — in which case this policy continues to apply to the
          information transferred.
        </p>

        <h2>Retention</h2>
        <p>
          We keep assessment submissions and contact records for as long as needed to serve you and
          to meet legal obligations, then delete or anonymize them. Consent records are retained
          longer where the law requires proof of consent. You may ask us to delete your information
          at any time.
        </p>

        <h2>Security</h2>
        <p>
          Traffic to this site is encrypted in transit, and access to submitted information is
          limited to people who need it. No method of transmission or storage is perfectly secure,
          so we cannot guarantee absolute security.
        </p>

        <h2>Your choices and rights</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Email:</strong> unsubscribe using the link in any message.</li>
          <li><strong>Text:</strong> reply STOP.</li>
          <li><strong>Access, correction, or deletion:</strong> email us and we will act on it.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          If you are a California resident, you may request the categories and specific pieces of
          personal information we have collected, request deletion or correction, and ask us not to
          sell or share your personal information. We do not sell or share personal information as
          those terms are used under California law. We will not discriminate against you for
          exercising these rights.
        </p>

        <h2>Children</h2>
        <p>
          This site is meant for businesses and is not directed to children under 16. We do not
          knowingly collect information from children. If you believe a child gave us information,
          contact us and we will delete it.
        </p>

        <h2>Changes</h2>
        <p>
          If we update this policy we will revise the effective date above. Material changes to how
          we handle your information will be made clear on this page.
        </p>

        <h2>Contact us</h2>
        <p>
          <strong>{LEGAL_ENTITY} d/b/a AITS</strong><br />
          {BUSINESS.city}, {BUSINESS.region}<br />
          Email: <a href={`mailto:${BUSINESS.email}`}>{BUSINESS.email}</a><br />
          Phone: <a href={`tel:${BUSINESS.phone}`}>{BUSINESS.phoneDisplay}</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .policy {
    color: var(--text2);
  }
  .policy h2 {
    font-family: var(--fran);
    font-size: clamp(19px, 2.2vw, 25px);
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--text);
    margin: 40px 0 12px;
  }
  .policy p {
    margin-bottom: 16px;
    line-height: 1.8;
  }
  .policy ul {
    margin: 0 0 16px 20px;
  }
  .policy li {
    margin-bottom: 8px;
    line-height: 1.75;
  }
  .policy strong {
    color: var(--text);
  }
  .callout {
    background: rgba(59, 110, 240, 0.06);
    border: 0.5px solid rgba(59, 110, 240, 0.28);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--accent);
    border-radius: 0 12px 12px 0;
    padding: 20px 24px;
    margin: 24px 0;
    line-height: 1.75;
  }
  .callout-strong {
    background: rgba(0, 201, 167, 0.05);
    border-color: rgba(0, 201, 167, 0.3);
    border-left-color: var(--teal);
  }
</style>
